      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nEnrolls every remaining step whose pytest commands set `PYTHONPATH`, with its AMD mirror, in automatic sharding. **Draft until ci-infra#825 merges**: setting `PYTHONPATH` replaces the path the sharding plugin is installed on, so today every shard of these steps fails with `No module named 'runtime_shard_plugin'` (seen in #62513's build 97706, which dropped Spec Decode for this reason). ci-infra#825 installs the plugin into site-packages, where a command's own `PYTHONPATH` can't hide it.\n\n## Claims\n\n| Step | Was | Planned shards |\n|---|---|---:|\n| `lm-eval-spec-decode-4xb200` | one job | 3 |\n| `entrypoints-integration-api-server` | 4 fixed shards | 5 |\n| `amd-entrypoints-integration-api-server` | 4 fixed shards | 4 |\n| `amd-lm-eval-spec-decode-4xb200` | one job | 2 |\n| `rust-frontend-serve-admin-coverage` | one job | 2 |\n| `amd-rust-frontend-serve-admin-coverage` | one job | 1 |\n\n- Every test runs exactly once across the shards, with the same environment and filters as before.\n- The API Server step's shard-1-only `dev/rpc` command and the `--num-shards/--shard-id` flags give way to the planner, so new test files no longer need placing by hand.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Planned each step and mirror on this branch with ci-infra main's planner and main's timings; the plans match the table.\n- Rendered each with the pipeline generator and ran every shard's commands against a mock test tree, as a PR build and in main's OTel mode: every test ran in exactly one shard (4/4 NVIDIA cases, 2/2 AMD mirror cases). That harness imports the plugin from an editable install, so it cannot show the `PYTHONPATH` problem; the `/ci run` after ci-infra#825 merges is the check for it.\n- Not run yet in CI: `/ci run`, plus a build scoped to the optional Spec Decode step and the AMD mirrors `/ci run` leaves out, once ci-infra#825 is merged.\n\n## Details\n\n- **Not duplicating an open PR.** #62513 dropped Spec Decode in favour of this one; no other open PR touches these keys.\n- **Spec Decode** has three configs, and one runs about 25 minutes on its own, so its slowest shard stays over the 20-minute target; the step's wait still roughly halves.\n- **API Server** goes from 4 fixed shards to 5 planned ones on the NVIDIA side. `entrypoints/serve/dev/rpc` now runs in whichever shard the plan gives it rather than always in shard 1. One file, `scale_out/ec_integration/test_scale_out_ec_e2e.py`, has no timing on main and is counted at the planner's default.\n- **Timeouts unchanged (human).** `timeout_in_minutes` stays per job; fallback-aware timeouts belong in a central timeout setting.\n- **One PR for the blocker.** Every enrollment that waits on ci-infra#825 is here, so they can all be validated with one `/ci run` once it merges.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n\n",
